1
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,000
The ultimate paradise

2
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,980
Easily leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,420
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,540
I wanna die with you one night

5
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:44,660
Don't just keep wearing the latest trends

6
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,200
Because you look far better
with your natural face

7
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,840
Let it ring

8
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:55,000
Everybody can do, we've started running

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

10
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's go regret things again tomorrow

11
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,380
Let it run

12
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

13
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,820
Even if we stick out, it doesn't hurt

14
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,000
Holding onto our rowdy curiosity

15
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,020
Reaching strong and high

16
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:30,780
With Zō-san

17
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,580
At the arcade until 10:30

18
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,380
Wait, let's make it 11 o'clock instead.

19
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:45,020
What have you been doing this whole time?

20
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:48,320
I thought you were Nakagawa or Chief Ohara.

21
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:52,068
I'm off tomorrow,
so I'm making a detailed schedule,

22
00:01:52,118 --> 00:01:53,700
and I'm going to spend a meaningful day.

23
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:56,380
You really do treasure your time outside of work,
don't you.

24
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,440
Of course.

25
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:00,900
There are far too few days
off compared to working days.

26
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:03,600
I want about five days off a week,
like everyone else.

27
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:06,000
By normal standards,
I get two days off a week.

28
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:09,000
I work hard for the safety of the citizens,
you know.

29
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:10,960
It's a reasonable request, isn't it?

30
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,980
But Ryo-chan's always got seven days off a week,
you know.

31
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,550
But to get through this
detailed schedule in full,

32
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,320
you'd need the stamina of an iron man.

33
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,320
Hello, this is Kameari.

34
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,500
What is it?

35
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:31,360
Let's take a break here, have lunch,
and have a face-to-face talk.

36
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,880
Senpai, it's an emergency!

37
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:33,500
Yeah.

38
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:43,440
It's dangerous, please step back.

39
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:45,000
Yes, step back, please.

40
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,960
Hey, you can't come in, please don't enter.

41
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:50,320
Please don't go in from here.

42
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,900
Please step back.

43
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,400
It's dangerous, so please step back.

44
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,260
Ready?

45
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,400
If you get stepped on, you end up like this.

46
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,860
Move, move, get out of the way.

47
00:02:59,020 --> 00:02:59,760
Too late.

48
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,020
Excuse me.

49
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,480
Nakagawa.

50
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,500
There isn't any!

51
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,700
So where is it? That elephant.

52
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,060
It's in the storage
room at the back, though.

53
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,900
Come on, go catch it quickly.

54
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,620
That's right.
You're used to this, aren't you?

55
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,680
Like hell I'm used to it.
Elephants, of all things!

56
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,060
I'll go with you.

57
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:24,080
Nakagawa's in danger.

58
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:26,060
What's that supposed to mean?
That's discrimination!

59
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,860
It's distinction, not discrimination.
Come on, hurry up and go.

60
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,160
What?

61
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,260
Here, take this.

62
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,480
Never mind, nothing.

63
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,780
It's just a kid.

64
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,580
See, it's okay, little elephant.

65
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,880
It's quiet, isn't it?
Do you think he'll be all right?

66
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:05,320
Senpai!

67
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,300
Nakagawa-san, it's dangerous!

68
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,480
Let go!

69
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:15,400
Let go of Senpai!

70
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,900
Eeeeeeh!

71
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:19,100
Eeeeeeh!

72
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,860
Nakagawa,
hurry and bring some milk and a baby bottle!

73
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,600
Hurry up!

74
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,240
Y-yes!

75
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,060
Nakagawa-san.

76
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,020
Nakagawa-san.

77
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,940
Thank goodness you're safe.

78
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,820
Excuse me,
do you have milk and a baby bottle?

79
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:58,360
!

80
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:58,620
It's ready!

81
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,020
I wonder if it'll even drink milk?

82
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,240
Milk is the basic food for all mammals,
isn't it?

83
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,160
Here, it's milk.

84
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,960
It's cow's milk, but please, bear with it.

85
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:17,200
Look, look, look, see, like this.

86
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:23,120
Come on, go on, try drinking it.

87
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,120
It drank it!

88
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:32,640
Good, good, what a good boy,
what a good boy.

89
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:43,940
The elephant's startled.

90
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:44,960
It's all right.

91
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,540
Don't be scared, don't be scared.

92
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:52,060
It's taken a real liking to Ryotsu Kankichi.

93
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,080
After all, it's a wild animal too.

94
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:56,320
It's big, but it's still a baby.

95
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,020
As long as we don't excite it,
it's quite docile.

96
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,860
But where did this elephant come from?

97
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:05,390
I can't imagine someone kept it as a pet,

98
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:08,660
and I can't imagine it swam
all the way from Africa either.

99
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,980
In that case, it's probably from a zoo.

100
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,040
I see.

101
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:15,860
Well, hold on to it here until they come to pick it up.
Let's go, Nakagawa.

102
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:18,760
Hey, come on, help me out here, Officer.

103
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:23,100
Ugh, shut up, Nakagawa!

104
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:28,900
No good, senpai, it won't let go!

105
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,460
This guy's dangerous.

106
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:32,200
What a perfect couple.

107
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,940
How did an elephant

108
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,160
end up lost, apparently?

109
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,920
And Ryo-chan is the one who picked it up.

110
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,340
Why is it in the police box's

111
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,600
storage room? If we tied it outside,
some drunk could get trampled, you know.

112
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,900
We have no choice but to
keep it here until morning.

113
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:55,760
Everyone's been so nice to it
that it's completely taken to them.

114
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:58,900
Ryotsu's always liked
by everyone except people

115
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,120
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

116
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,400
See?

117
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,460
Wow, it's the real thing. It's huge!

118
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,400
Pay 100 yen and I'll let you ride it.

119
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,120
Wow, really?

120
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,600
Ryotsu!

121
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,120
I'm kidding.

122
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,940
Free, it's free. Go on, try it.

123
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,360
Yay! Hey, let me ride, let me ride!

124
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,580
Fine, fine. Here we go.

125
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,040
Wow, that's amazing.

126
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,480
It's so tall!

127
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:26,460
Big brother, you gave it grass.

128
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:27,900
No way!

129
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,480
Hasn't a missing person report been filed?

130
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,560
We did report it to headquarters,
but so far there's been nothing...

131
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,220
Well then,

132
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:39,820
If it starts fussing again,
give it some more milk.

133
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:42,500
You're not seriously going home,
are you, senpai?

134
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,280
Alright, senpai!

135
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:47,420
What's going on? What's going on?

136
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:51,700
Why are you all looking at me like that?

137
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,980
My shift is over, so

138
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:57,180
I'm officially off duty
until tomorrow, right?

139
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,480
You'd just be lounging
around all day anyway.

140
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:02,520
Why don't you take care of this
thing until they come to pick it up?

141
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:03,720
No.

142
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:05,440
What?

143
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:09,420
Apparently this is Senpai's
schedule for his day off tomorrow.

144
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,800
It's packed, down to the minute.

145
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,298
Wake up at 9:00, breakfast at 9:03,

146
00:08:14,348 --> 00:08:16,260
9:30, model kits.

147
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:20,460
10:45 a.m. morning service

148
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,200
Come on, it's already late.

149
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:22,940
You two should head home.

150
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,840
12:00 lunch

151
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,740
That's how it is.

152
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:29,440
He's only methodical when
it comes to trivial things.

153
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,860
That's far too irresponsible.

154
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:34,020
If you brought it here, you have to
take care of it properly until the end.

155
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,360
That's right, Ryo-chan.

156
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,120
Hey, that's not my statue!

157
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:40,380
We didn't bring it here.
It followed us on its own.

158
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:43,680
Do you expect me to stay quiet while
my precious day off gets ruined by this?

159
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:44,880
Good work.

160
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,500
See you.

161
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,480
I'm going home no matter what!

162
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,600
No matter what anyone says, I'm going home.

163
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,860
Let go! I said let go!

164
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:12,300
It won't let go of you, senpai.

165
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,760
Why don't you take it with you, Yocchan?

166
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:16,320
Don't be stupid.

167
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,760
Do that, Ryotsu.

168
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,560
This is an order from the Chief.

169
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,940
W-what's that big thing, Ryo-san?

170
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,400
It's an order from the Chief.

171
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,220
If you have a complaint,
take it up with Chief Ohara.

172
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,540
I just cleaned the floor, you know.

173
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,940
Please don't go running around!

174
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:47,560
Oh my, it's fine, right? Oh my.

175
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,500
Excuse me for a moment.

176
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,520
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

177
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,500
Don't go putting it in the bath.

178
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,820
It's Auntie's orders.

179
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,680
If you've got a complaint,
take it up with Auntie.

180
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,820
Okay, the other way.

181
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,440
Okay, now the back.

182
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,780
There, it's clean now

183
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:20,540
Listen, you wait here quietly.

184
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,080
For some reason, this guy only
seems to understand what I say.

185
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,000
Come on, it's fine.

186
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:36,620
You don't understand at all, Ryo-san.

187
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,640
Please, just don't roll over!

188
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,400
What's wrong?

189
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:03,600
Wait, what?

190
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:08,720
Hey!

191
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,200
Hey, trainee! That's my breakfast!

192
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:18,640
What are we supposed to
eat for breakfast now?

193
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,680
This happened because Ryo-san
brought an elephant in here.

194
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,680
If you're its owner, take responsibility.

195
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,800
I keep telling you,
this elephant isn't mine!

196
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,080
Do something about it, Ryo-san!

197
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:33,200
Listen, stop complaining and get
them to send a pickup right now.

198
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:37,520
But no one has reported a
missing elephant yet, so...

199
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:41,780
Then where did it come from?
Is it a stray elephant?

200
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,480
In that case, contact the health center.

201
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:49,780
Anyway, I'll let you know as soon as we get any information,
so until then, please hang on.

202
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:55,240
Honestly, every last one of you is
taking advantage of my kind nature!

203
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:14,180
Serves you right!
Straight to the 9:30 model kit section!

204
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:22,060
Hey, that thing you wanted just came in.

205
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:22,840
Really?

206
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:26,000
The Douglas A1 Skyraider from Morogram.

207
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,680
This is it. This is the one I wanted.

208
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,220
That'll be eight thousand yen, right?

209
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:34,380
I forgot my wallet, Ryo.

210
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,580
Here you go again with that.

211
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:40,220
No, really! I'll bring that money next time.

212
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:42,440
Ryo-san?

213
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:51,740
So they've already come.
The back door's this way.

214
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:54,180
Whoa, no helping me, Ryo-san.

215
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:57,500
Two others have also called,
insisting they must have it.

216
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,320
If you want it, bring the money.

217
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,182
That's a bit one-sided, isn't it.

218
00:13:01,232 --> 00:13:04,840
I'll definitely pay, so don't sell it!
Please, I'm begging you.

219
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:05,920
No way.

220
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,260
I'm not getting caught.

221
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:25,100
Are you a police dog or something?

222
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:30,440
Why do I have to go on a date with
an elephant on my precious day off?

223
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:37,700
Fine, do it yourself. I don't know you.

224
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,780
Running around made me so thirsty.

225
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:50,720
Damn, if only I had 10 more yen.

226
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:52,820
10 more yen.

227
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:55,640
There's Tsubutsubu Grape right there!

228
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,760
Tsubutsubu Grape.

229
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:03,740
Tsubutsubu.

230
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:06,540
10 yen.

231
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:13,730
For small amounts of change,
even if you bring it to the police box,

232
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:16,600
it's hard to identify the owner.

233
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,760
If the owner comes back right away,
just give it back.

234
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,960
There, there, you did it. Good, good.

235
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,980
Then, Tsubutsubu Grape.

236
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:27,460
You went and ruined the oshiruko!

237
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:30,420
How am I supposed to drink
oshiruko when I'm this thirsty?

238
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:32,160
Pay back my 100 yen, you bastard.

239
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:40,840
Two more bottles?

240
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:45,500
If we're going to, get something else out.

241
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:50,180
Even though it only
makes us thirstier, we keep

242
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:52,900
going back for our wallets is a hassle too.

243
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,780
Looks like the ten o'clock plan is canceled.

244
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:58,020
Thanks to you, we missed breakfast too,

245
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,000
and my carefully planned
day-off schedule is ruined.

246
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:07,060
So what should we do
with the rest of the day?

247
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:09,980
Did you find another one?

248
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:12,180
It's a wallet.

249
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:14,360
And it's heavy, too.

250
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,340
Isn't that Daiki?

251
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:19,880
That wallet!

252
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,840
We've been looking for it.

253
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,900
Thank you, you've saved me.

254
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:26,580
What proof do you have
that this is your wallet?

255
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,540
I'm sure there's a photo of
me with my grandchild inside,

256
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,480
but unfortunately,
that's the only thing I can offer as proof.

257
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:40,020
Carrying around that much cash
isn't something I'd admire.

258
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:42,040
Thank you, I'll be careful.

259
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:44,840
But what an unusual pet.

260
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:48,800
In Asia,
elephants have long been regarded as gods,

261
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:52,240
and I hear many countries cherish them.

262
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:53,660
A god? This one?

263
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:56,060
It's a small amount, I'm sorry to say,

264
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,660
but please use it for the elephant's feed.

265
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,520
This much?

266
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:03,740
Ten percent is the usual reward, isn't it?

267
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,580
Well then, good day.

268
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:09,060
Look, there's 30,000 yen here!

269
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,540
Looks like it followed us.

270
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:16,160
In that case,
back to the afternoon schedule!

271
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,320
Keep up, you hear, god.

272
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,180
How much is a ticket for an elephant?

273
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:26,700
There are no tickets for elephants.

274
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,080
So it's free, then.

275
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:29,700
Apparently it's free.

276
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:55,380
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...
Ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii ii

277
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:00,680
Hey, sir!

278
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:08,040
Sir?

279
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:11,800
The train for Platform
2 will arrive shortly.

280
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,520
Hurry, the train's coming!

281
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:26,960
Let those getting off go first!

282
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:37,120
Excuse me, could you scoot in a bit?

283
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:55,980
Aaaaaaah!

284
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,940
It's not coming in at all, damn it!

285
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:05,920
What god?
That old geezer got my hopes up for nothing!

286
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:09,980
This is my last 1,000 yen.

287
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:13,440
If this misses, we'll have to
walk all the way back to Kameari!

288
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:18,820
If 47 comes in, it pays twenty times!

289
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:22,200
But then,
there's the 36 combination to consider, too.

290
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:26,160
There are people waiting behind you,
so please line up again once you've decided.

291
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:34,040
The sixth race will start shortly.

292
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:40,040
Okay, let's play it safe, go for the No. 2 main line,
and keep our hopes up for the next race.

293
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,520
It's No. 2.

294
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:45,160
Class one, right?

295
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:47,200
No, no, not class one. Number two!

296
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,340
Next person, please.

297
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:54,280
3,738,100 yen!

298
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:01,620
Hey, staff! Babysitting duty is piling up!

299
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:10,100
I've never heard of this! Both of them are unranked rescue races, aren't they?!
They're switching these nobody horses around depending on the distance!

300
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,480
This 100-yen god!

301
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,840
A god! You're a god, aren't you?!

302
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:26,140
No way!

303
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:32,020
We won!

304
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:35,820
We got it! We hit the big payout!

305
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:38,860
We got it!

306
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,080
You...

307
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,220
You're worth money!

308
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:02,900
Here you go, Ryo-san!

309
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,880
Look, a brand-new car!

310
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:20,140
Sorry about that.
You were a wonderful elephant.

311
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:25,800
Alright, to thank you for this big win,
I'll treat you to anything you want.

312
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:31,800
Ryo-chan,
where on earth did he go with that elephant?

313
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:37,500
Hello, this is Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

314
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:39,340
What, you saw an elephant!

315
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:51,860
I've got a feeling you and I are going
to be good friends for a long time.

316
00:20:58,020 --> 00:20:58,880
That's cold!

317
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:01,580
You really went and did it

318
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,240
Hey, you little rascal.

319
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:12,060
Now that I look closer,
you've got a cute face.

320
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:29,140
Tonto!

321
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,240
Tonto?

322
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,060
Ryotsu!

323
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:33,800
Chief!

324
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:37,340
What were you thinking,
dragging an elephant around town!

325
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:41,920
Before noon, a missing-animal search
request came in from the Ueno Zoo,

326
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,860
and the police box got a call about it.

327
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,160
Ryo-chan has gone missing too.

328
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:49,360
Anyway,
I'm glad the elephant and Senpai are safe.

329
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,800
Sorry for the trouble.

330
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:57,260
Apparently Tonto's mother
passed away yesterday.

331
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:03,900
We zookeepers were so
busy nursing our mothers

332
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,720
that we completely forgot about Tonto,

333
00:22:07,940 --> 00:22:11,120
and apparently he got lonely
by himself and escaped his cage.

334
00:22:12,020 --> 00:22:14,280
Thank you so much for taking care of Tonto.

335
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:17,060
What are you going on about?

336
00:22:18,180 --> 00:22:20,640
Hey! What do you think
you're doing to my head!

337
00:22:20,920 --> 00:22:21,380
No, no.

338
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:23,520
What are you doing?!

339
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:24,860
Let go of me for a second!

340
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:26,640
There, there, are you all right?!

341
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:27,380
Don't be scared!

342
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,020
What are you doing?!

343
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:30,860
Look, Chief,
he doesn't like it either, right?

344
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:32,440
I'll buy this one.

345
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:34,620
Bakabon, Nakagawa, come here!

346
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:35,660
Y-yes!

347
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:36,920
Hahaha!

348
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:37,500
Let go of me, please.

349
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:38,560
Senpai.

350
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,520
Nakagawa, whatever you do, don't let go!

351
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:43,200
Come on, it's dangerous,
so let's do this while we still can.

352
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,980
Yes, we need your cooperation.

353
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:47,780
Alright, leave it to me.

354
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,840
One, two...

355
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:52,800
One, two...

356
00:22:58,860 --> 00:23:01,340
Stop it! Stop it!

357
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:03,600
Stop! Let go!
Is it so hard to understand now?

358
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:08,720
Tonto is my elephant!

359
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,665
Ryo-chan's kind heart,

360
00:23:12,715 --> 00:23:16,520
even when you go back to the zoo,
I'm sure we'll never forget you, Tonto-chan.

361
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:21,640
Tonto!

362
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,200
Wait, Tonton!

363
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:25,340
Aaaaaah!

364
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:26,520
Wait!

365
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:28,580
Tonton!

366
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,400
Senpai...

367
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:33,860
Ryo-chan may look like that, but he
really does have a kind heart, doesn't he.

368
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:35,980
Tonton!

369
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:38,340
Tell me!

370
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:41,360
What's going to win the next Emperor's Cup?!

371
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:47,180
We should just have that guy
win along with us at the zoo, too.

372
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:49,300
Tonton!

373
00:23:50,140 --> 00:23:52,140
If the Emperor's Cup is no good,
then what about the Arima Kinen?

374
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:54,140
No, what's going to win the Derby?

375
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:06,800
Did you fall for Megumi
at the Aijo Bento shop?

376
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:08,860
Good, well done, Honda, you did great!

377
00:24:09,180 --> 00:24:11,440
Third time's the charm,
you've got to get her this time!

378
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:14,500
Leave it to me, a special, experienced,
nice middle-aged guy like myself,

379
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,500
I'll teach you the key points for a date.

380
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:20,680
Next time, run, Honda, for love. Good luck!

381
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:32,660
Even if you stop the clock,

382
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,740
time keeps passing by.

383
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,700
Don't keep that sour face,

384
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:48,000
let's laugh it off and go on living.

385
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today is rainy,

386
00:24:59,380 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

387
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye.

388
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,820
Say goodbye to the bad things.

389
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's try living as we please.

390
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,940
Good things will come.

391
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:30,220
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

392
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

